{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3978","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3978","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3978\",\"parent_revision\":\"08e20ebf185e02e1c3b1283763bca27a3d953388\",\"root_revision\":\"259dcd5c63f7c347ed6b65d8dd5d44c356f7adbf5504c5b0e655ea29877c66f5\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: in-progress\\nadded: 2026-09-27\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA REST 403 for the primary rate limit ('API rate limit exceeded', RateLimitExceededException, often without a Retry-After header) is classified NON_RETRYABLE by sync_state._classify_github_exception. Sync then goes OFFLINE and MCP responses report retryable: false while the limit is only temporary. Found by Codex on #3968 (PRRT_kwDOQGimCs6mbw5i); the behaviour predates #3968.\\n\\nUser-provided context: classify RateLimitExceededException as retryable before the generic 403 rule, and take the delay from x-ratelimit-reset when Retry-After is absent.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-27T22:11:29.438897Z</sub>\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: A REST 403 for the primary rate limit ('API rate limit exceeded', RateLimitExceededException, often without a Retry-After header) is classified NON_RETRYABLE by sync_state._classify_github_exception.\\nevidence: Source code inspection of _classify_github_exception (backlog_core/sync_state.py lines 352-379, commit 6befa35e3 onward): the 403 branch checks for Retry-After header and \\\"secondary rate limit\\\" message marker, but contains no check for exhausted x-ratelimit-remaining header or \\\"API rate limit exceeded\\\" message text. When neither condition is true, it returns NON_RETRYABLE (line 376). This classification applies to any 403 lacking a Retry-After header and without \\\"secondary rate limit\\\" in the message, including primary rate-limit exhaustions identified by x-ratelimit-remaining==0. The gh_client._is_rate_limited helper (lines 892-916) correctly identifies primary rate limits via RateLimitExceededException or x-ratelimit-remaining exhaustion for GraphQL paths, but sync_state does not use this check for REST responses.\\nsource: file:///Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/sync_state.py:352-379 (lines 371-376 showing 403 classification logic)\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: the behaviour predates #3968\\nevidence: Git history shows commit 6befa35e3 (\\\"fix(dh): stop GitHub requests hanging and classify rate limits as retryable (#3968)\\\") introduced logic checking for \\\"secondary rate limit\\\" in message and Retry-After header. Before that commit (parent 6befa35e3~1), 403 classification was: `headers: dict[str, str] = exc.headers or {}; return SyncErrorKind.RETRYABLE if \\\"Retry-After\\\" in headers else SyncErrorKind.NON_RETRYABLE`. The current code (unchanged since 6befa35e3) still does not handle primary-rate-limit 403s specifically, confirming the original behavior predates #3968. The issue was not introduced by #3968 but rather coexisted with its secondary-rate-limit fix.\\nsource: git show 6befa35e3~1:plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/sync_state.py sed -n '330,340p' (pre-#3968 code); git log --oneline shows 6befa35e3 is the #3968 commit; current code identical in 403 handling\\n\\nverdict: INCONCLUSIVE\\nclaim: Found by Codex on #3968 (PRRT_kwDOQGimCs6mbw5i)\\nevidence: The reference \\\"PRRT_kwDOQGimCs6mbw5i\\\" is a GitHub PR discussion thread ID, not a standalone issue. Attempting to read issue #3968 returns 404 (\\\"Could not resolve to an Issue with the number of 3968\\\"). Commit 6befa35e3 exists with message \\\"fix(dh): stop GitHub requests hanging and classify rate limits as retryable (#3968)\\\" and addresses secondary, not primary, rate limits. Without access to the PR discussion thread content or a linked issue, I cannot verify whether Codex found the primary-rate-limit 403 problem within #3968 discussions or whether this is a newly identified related issue. The claim statement is unclear: does \\\"found by Codex on #3968\\\" mean discovered while working on that issue, or discovered and reported in that thread?\\nsource: unavailable \u2014 GitHub PR discussion thread ID requires authentication; issue #3968 resolves to PR commit 6befa35e3 (secondary rate limit fix, not primary)\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Sync then goes OFFLINE and MCP responses report retryable: false while the limit is only temporary.\\nevidence: SyncStatus.OFFLINE state is entered when a sync failure is classified NON_RETRYABLE (sync_engine delegates classification to classify_sync_error, which uses _classify_github_exception for GithubException). When a primary-rate-limit 403 without Retry-After header is classified NON_RETRYABLE, sync transitions to OFFLINE (sync_state.py lines 85-86 and state machine behavior). MCP responses report retryable field based on SyncErrorKind classification through server._failure_verdict, propagating the NON_RETRYABLE verdict. The rate limit is temporary by GitHub's definition (temporary exhaustion of remaining quota), but the code treats it as permanent.\\nsource: file:///Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/sync_state.py:85-93 (SyncStatus enum), server.py _failure_verdict, classify_sync_error function logic\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-27T22:01:42.736351Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: Primary-quota 403 rate limit is classified non-retryable\\nDate: 2026-09-28\\nGoal: A primary-quota 403 (RateLimitExceededException / exhausted x-ratelimit-remaining) classifies as RETRYABLE with a delay from x-ratelimit-reset when Retry-After is absent.\\nConditions:\\n1. Location of the misclassification (sync_state._classify_github_exception, 403 branch) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Existing rate-limit detection helper to reuse (gh_client._is_rate_limited) and the import-direction constraint between gh_client and sync_state | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. How a retry delay flows from the classifier to the scheduler / MCP retryable field | Status: DERIVABLE\\n4. Shape of GitHub primary-limit 403 responses (headers present, message text) | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 2\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-27T22:07:05.787449Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n**Rationale**: Traceable failure with identifiable cause chain. RateLimitExceededException (temporary GitHub primary-quota 403) is misclassified as non-retryable due to generic 403 rule executing before exception-type-specific check. Reproduction: primary rate limit exhaustion during sync. Fix location is known (sync_state._classify_github_exception).\\n**Analysis Method**: 5-whys\\n**Scenario Target**: Primary GitHub rate limit (temporary, always resolves in 60 seconds) incorrectly pauses sync as if it were a permanent auth error \u2192 Primary rate limit is recognized as retryable with correct delay extracted from x-ratelimit-reset header\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session 2026-09-27: live e2e / GitHub robustness work (#3968, #3969, #3975)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-27\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-27T22:07:05.787494Z</sub>\\n\\n**Method**: 5-whys via item description\\n**Evidence chain**:\\n1. Observed failure: RateLimitExceededException from GitHub primary-quota 403 is classified NON_RETRYABLE; sync transitions OFFLINE\\n2. Why: sync_state._classify_github_exception matches the HTTP 403 status to NON_RETRYABLE\\n3. Why: No RateLimitExceededException-specific classification check exists before the generic 403 rule\\n4. Why: Classification logic orders generic patterns (status codes) before specific exception types\\n5. Why: Code was written with broad-match-first strategy instead of narrow-before-broad exception hierarchy\\n**Root cause**: Exception classification uses generic-before-specific pattern matching, allowing temporary rate-limit 403s to be misclassified as permanent auth failures.\\n**Fix locus**: sync_state._classify_github_exception, 403 branch \u2014 add RateLimitExceededException check before generic 403 rule; extract delay from x-ratelimit-reset when Retry-After absent\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"478201174e7cb39f6cb435b7b7546a173206173be6003ed5b57c2909d5b1182c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXU1jUw\",\"fields\":{\"stack\":\"\",\"status\":\"in-progress\",\"item_type\":\"Bug\",\"priority\":\"P1\",\"added\":\"2026-09-27\",\"files\":\"\",\"followup_to\":\"\",\"layer\":\"\",\"research_first\":\"\",\"close_reference\":\"\",\"source\":\"Session 2026-09-27: live e2e / GitHub robustness work (#3968, #3969, #3975)\",\"groomed\":\"2026-09-27\",\"topic\":\"\",\"close_comment\":\"\",\"plan\":\"\",\"language\":\"\",\"suggested_location\":\"\",\"close_reason\":\"\"}}"}